  "$schemaComment": "SSOT for v2 mechanisms. `networks` holds network identity, env keys, and default pricing. `routes` holds one canonical definition per paid HTTP path (payment requirements, declared extensions, and `sdks` listing which SDKs implement it). Handlers always return `{ message: \"Protected endpoint accessed successfully\", timestamp }`. Servers derive middleware config and handlers from this file; nothing is hardcoded per framework. Legacy v1 is out of scope.",
